Suppose a sentence has these three tokens. This code builds one input-target pair; it does not tokenize text or train a model.

```javascript
const tokens = ["The", "bird", "sang"];
const input = tokens.slice(0, 2);
const target = tokens[2];
console.log(input.join(" "));
console.log(target);
```

It prints The bird, then sang. The target was already in the text.
